{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And the land shall not be sold in perpetuity.</b> This teaches you that if the purchaser holds on to this field and does not return it to its owners in the Jubilee, he transgresses this negative prohibition. The term צמיתות means a cut-off and absolute sale, and likewise the Targum renders it לחלוטין." "<b>For the land is Mine.</b> Do not let your eye grow evil toward it, for the world is Mine and I so desire — thus did the Sages of blessed memory expound." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: 'for the land is Mine' — it is destined to return to Me in the Jubilee. And to this King David, peace be upon him, alluded in his saying (Psalms 24:1): ״לה׳ הארץ ומלואה״. And the intent of the opening of the psalm, which begins with the letter lamed — which is the greatest of all the letters, and which the masters of truth call 'the flying tower (מגדל הפורח באויר)' — will not be hidden from you, once you understand what we have written above. Or one may say: 'to Me the land' — the upper land; and in the seventh year it does not act in the lower land, and it is as though the lower land is not Mine — therefore let it not be yours." "<b>And this is</b> what they said in the Midrash: 'for you are strangers and sojourners with Me' — do not make yourselves the owners. 'You are with Me' — it is enough for the servant to be like his master: when it is Mine, then it is yours. And the explanation of this is: when it is Mine during the other years, when it acts in the land, then it is yours; but in the seventh year, when it does not act in the land and it is as though it is not Mine — therefore let it not be yours, for it is enough for the servant to be like his master. And this is clear."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:28:27.699466994Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}